  "marketingText": "Kayfabizarro: PLATO'S DUNGEON RAIDS – Western Philosophy as a Trap-Filled Crawl (Free Cut & Play Comic Card Game)\n\nWestern philosophy is a haunted house somebody filed the warning labels off of. Every doorway is an idea, and about half of them bite.\n\nThis deck refuses to do what your reading list did to you. It will not hand you a tidy lineage of great men nodding at each other across the centuries. It will not let an argument sit safely behind glass with a date stamped under it. It will not pretend that GASLIGHT, ROKO'S BASILISK, and the TOWER OF MEDIA are antique curiosities instead of the exact traps working on you between breakfast and lunch. The fallacies are not on the syllabus here. They are the monsters in the corridor, and you have to name them out loud before they name you.\n\nSo you raid it. You pick a thinker, you walk the zones from the character cards down to the endgame, and at every turn the table decides whether your idea held its ground or got exposed as a cheap costume. This is Social Story Wrestling with a dungeon underneath: 49 cut-and-play cards, real philosophy rebuilt as rooms you can clear, traps you can spring, and one rabbit narrating the body count.\n\nWHAT'S INSIDE?\n- The Raid Core Deck: 49 High-Res \"Print, Cut & Play\" Cards, featuring GASLIGHT, ROKO'S BASILISK, and the TOWER OF MEDIA, plus a full map zone called The Digestive Tract of History to crawl through.\n- The Freestyle Rules: The complete Anti-Rulebook. No complicated math, just storytelling, the R/A/F dice driving the chaos, and a penalty system for when your logic collapses mid-bit.\n- The Fallacy Engine: every classic trap built as a creature with a stat block, so you stop reciting the names of bad arguments and start fighting them across a folding table.\n\nTHE \"LIVING DECK\" PASS (Free Updates)\nThis is Set 02 of the Krazy Kayfabizarro main series. Grab it and you are not buying a frozen PDF, you are on the line for the whole cycle. Every future expansion and topic deck in this run lands in your lap as a free update.\n\nWHY \"PAY WHAT YOU WANT\"?\nI draw these because a fallacy you can picture is a fallacy you can dodge, and most people were never once shown the picture. Broke? Enter \"0\" and take it. Run it in a classroom, an improv room, a kitchen full of people who think they already won the argument. Want to support the craft? Every dollar goes straight into drawing the next deck.\n\nChoose your reality. Become an Epistemic Outlaw.\n\"An idea you cannot picture is an idea that gets to keep hunting you.\"\nStay fluffy. — Uncle FrizzleBob",
